    "No direct torasemide-in-cirrhosis bioavailability record is present in the supplied cards.",
    "Query-specific permeability, solubility, and first-pass extraction are not experimentally measured; the low prior is physicochemical only.",
    "Cirrhosis severity and the query's formulation/dose are unspecified; cirrhosis records used different drugs, doses, and formulations.",
    "Transfer from bumetanide/tolfenamic acid/isradipine relies on structural and condition analogy rather than identical-molecule data.",
    "Some new low-F records are from non-cirrhotic, non-human, or formulation-specific settings and cannot be quantitatively transferred."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%): all transferable cirrhosis-context records—bumetanide 95–100%, tolfenamic acid ~100% (91–126%), and isradipine 28–37%—are above threshold; new L2 records reinforce this pattern. The physicochemical low prior is not affirmative evidence of F < 20%, and the low-F L2 records are from unrelated molecules, species, or formulations. Confidence remains high; revision strengthened."
}

